 </exercise> 
 <p>
    In the following, suppose that A and B are events in a sample space S. 
 </p>
<exercise workspace="1in">
    <statement>
        <p>
            If <m>P(A)=0.3. P(B)=0.8</m> and <m>P(A\cup B)=0.95</m>, then find <m>P(A \cap B)</m>.
        </p>
    </statement>
</exercise>
</page>
<page>
<exercise workspace="1in">
    <statement>
        <p>
            If <m>P(A')=0.4. P(B)=0.5</m> and <m>P(A\cap B)=0.4</m>, then find <m>P(A \cup B)</m>.
        </p>
      
    </statement>
</exercise>

<exercise workspace="1.5in">
    <statement>
        <p>
            If <m>P(A\cap B)=0.1. P(A\cap B')=0.3</m> and <m>P(A\cup B)=0.8</m>, then find <m>P(B)</m>.
        </p>
       
    </statement>
</exercise>

